OL,3,GNEWSAChannel Islands fuel prices set to
OL,4,Arise again
OL,5,
OL,6,FFuel prices are set to rise in a move
OL,7,Fwhich will likely see diesel cost more
OL,8,Fthan #2 per litre.
OL,10,FNick Crolla, head of marketing for
OL,11,FChannel Islands supplier Rubis, said:
OL,12,F"We have seen global fuel market prices
OL,13,Fincrease by nearly 30% since the end of
OL,14,FAugust. These increases are now
OL,15,Fbeginning to filter through to the
OL,16,Flocal market and will be reflected at
OL,17,Fforecourts over coming weeks."
OL,19,FHe added: "While these factors are
OL,20,Foutside our control, we are doing
OL,21,Feverything possible to keep prices as
OL,22,Flow as possible."
OL,23,APub: 29-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
